Lesson Learned

I learned the importance of preparing and updating the weekly report continuously throughout the week instead of waiting until the last minute. Regular updates help ensure the report is accurate, complete, and submitted on time.

RCA (Root Cause Analysis)

1. I underestimated the effort required to complete the weekly report. I initially thought it would only take about 30 minutes, but since it was my first time writing this type of report, I was unfamiliar with the expected level of detail and structure.

2. My time management was not effective. I postponed the report until the end of the week, which made it more difficult to recall all activities accurately and complete the report on time.

3. I also experienced technical issues due to an unstable internet connection, which affected my ability to work efficiently and submit the report promptly.

Corrective Actions

1. I will create the weekly report at the beginning of each week and update it daily with the tasks, knowledge, and progress made during the day.

2. At the end of the week, I will review and consolidate all updates to ensure the report is complete and accurate before submission.

3. I will allocate dedicated time for preparing the report instead of leaving it until the deadline.

4. To reduce the impact of network issues, I will prepare the report offline when necessary and synchronize or submit it once the connection is stable.